  "limitations": [
    "Reverse-sorted input roughly doubles comparison work; sorted and all-tied input add only selected heap pops but still retain a work tradeoff.",
    "Missing-heavy inventories may consume most of the ranked tail; no worst-case throughput improvement is claimed.",
    "Heap construction remains O(inventory) with 32-byte entries. Discovery, catalog loading, index preparation and final serialization are unchanged.",
    "Heap snapshots exclude inventory construction, C/native memory, mapped pages, stacks, allocator overhead and physical memory. They are rank/projection controls, not complete CLI memory or latency.",
    "No CPU or elapsed-time threshold is a test gate."
  ],
